msgid "pandas marks a missing value with `NaN` in number columns, and with `NaN` or `None` in text columns (pandas 3: `NaN` in the `str` type). Nullable types (`Int64`, [lecture 13](./13-numpy-pandas-intro.md#whole-numbers-with-missing-values-int64)) use `pd.NA`. Do not compare with them - use `isna()` / `notna()`:"
