msgid "Unlike NumPy ([lecture 13](./13-numpy-pandas-intro.md#missing-values-in-numpy-nan)), pandas skips `NaN` in `sum`, `mean`, `min`, `max` - like SQL and SAS `PROC MEANS`:"
msgstr ""

#. box title
#: site/lectures/14-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:847
msgid "A mean that skips is a different mean"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/14-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:848
msgid "`mean()` divides by the values that are there (398 here), not by all rows. If a missing amount means 0, fill it first - that changes the mean. Decide what a missing value means before you aggregate."
